  <setup>
    <math name="k"><selectFromSequence from="12" to="18" step="1"/></math>
    <!-- <math name="b"><selectFromSequence from="0.25" to="0.75" step="0.25"/></math>
    <math name="c"><selectFromSequence from="1" to="3" step="1"/></math> -->
    <function name="s" symbolic="true" domain="[0,$lands]" variable="t">
      <label>s</label>
      -4.9t^2 + $k
    </function>
    <derivative name="v">$s</derivative>
    <derivative name="a">$v</derivative>

    <math name="lands" simplify>sqrt($k/4.9)</math>

  </setup>
  <p>
    A ball is dropped from a window.  The ball's height (in meters) at time <m>t</m> (in seconds) is given by  the function <m>s(t) = $$s(t) </m>.  Recall that the ball's velocity is given by the instantaneous rate of change of its height, and the ball's acceleration is the instantaneous rate of change of its velocity.<!-- <math>$$h(t)</math> -->
  </p>

  <p>
    For each of the following prompts, note that you must choose units (using the provided drop-down menus) that match with the quantity you determine. 
  </p>

<!--
    <figure>
      <graph xmin="-1" xmax="3" ymin="-2" ymax="20" size="medium" grid="false" showNavigation="false"> $h $A $B  </graph>
      <caption>Plot of <m>y = h(t)</m>, which measures the height in meters of the falling ball at time <m>t</m> in seconds.</caption>
    </figure>
-->

  <ol marker="a">
      <li>
        <p>
          Use appropriate derivative shortcut rules to find formulas for the ball's velocity, <m>v(t)</m>, and acceleration, <m>a(t)</m>.  In addition, select the corresponding units for each.
        </p>
        <p>
            <m>v(t)=</m><answer name="vel"><award>$v</award></answer><answer><choiceInput name="choice1" inline>
              <choice>feet</choice>
              <choice>seconds</choice>
              <choice>meters</choice>
              <choice>feet per second</choice>
              <choice credit="1">meters per second</choice>
              <choice>meters per hour</choice>
            </choiceInput></answer>
        </p>
        <!-- <feedback condition = "$vel.creditAchieved != 1 and $vel.responseHasBeenSubmitted">Recall that the velocity <m>v(t)</m> is the rate of change (or derivative) of the position function <m>s(t)</m>.</feedback> -->
        <p>
            <m>a(t)=</m><answer name="acc"><award>$a</award></answer><answer><choiceInput name="choice2" inline>
              <choice>meters per hour</choice>
              <choice>meters per hour per hour</choice>
              <choice>feet per second per second</choice>
              <choice>meters per second</choice>
              <choice credit="1">meters per second per second</choice>
            </choiceInput></answer>
        </p>
        <!-- <feedback condition = "$acc.creditAchieved != 1 and $acc.responseHasBeenSubmitted">Recall that the acceleration <m>a(t)</m> is the rate of change (or derivative) of the velocity function <m>v(t)</m>.</feedback> -->
      </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Find the exact time the ball lands, and call this value <m>t_{\text{lands}}</m>.  In addition, select the corresponding units for this quantity.
      </p>
      <p>
         <m>t_{\text{lands}}=</m><answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><award>$lands</award></answer><answer><choiceInput name="choice3" inline>
              <choice>feet</choice>
              <choice credit="1">seconds</choice>
              <choice>meters</choice>
              <choice>feet per second</choice>
              <choice>meters per second</choice>
              <choice>meters per hour</choice>
            </choiceInput></answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
         The ball's instantaneous velocity <m>1</m> second before it lands is
      </p>
      <p><answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.02" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><award>$$v($lands-1)</award></answer><answer>
            <choiceInput name="choice4" inline>
              <choice>meters per hour</choice>
              <choice>meters</choice>
              <choice>feet per second</choice>
              <choice credit="1">meters per second</choice>
              <choice>feet</choice>
            </choiceInput>
          </answer>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>